{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>ויקרבו ימי</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other concerning David. It is found in the Midrash: The Holy One, blessed be He, said: You composed 147 psalms (aside from Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun), equal to the number of the years of Jacob — may you merit like him: just as he and his son reigned together, so too Solomon your son shall reign in your lifetime. Another interpretation: just as Jacob did not reach the days of his fathers, so too David, as it is written of him: והמלך דוד זקן בא בימים וגו׳ (\"And King David was old, advanced in days, etc.\")." "<b>נא ידך</b> In gematria: מילה." "<b>חסד ואמת</b> Rashi explained: חסד that one does for the dead — this is אמת." "<b>אמת</b> Notarikon: ארון מטה תכריכין."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "The verse והמלך דוד זקן בא בימים is from I Kings 1:1, which the Ba'al HaTurim left unaddressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:34.071996116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}